{{--
  The WildLoop mark: a closed ring with the runner's position on it.

  Pure CSS on purpose, so the wordmark never depends on icon resolution the way
  the rest of the UI's glyphs do — and one component, because it did not used to
  be. The nav, footer, and mobile header drew the ring-and-dot; the three auth
  pages drew a DIFFERENT shape, a 3/4 ring with `border-t-transparent`, which
  reads as a loading spinner rather than a logo and rendered as nothing at all
  next to the wordmark. Sign-in is the first page a logged-out visitor sees, so
  that was the one place the brand had to be right and the one place it wasn't.
--}}
<span
  class="relative inline-block shrink-0 rounded-full border-2 border-emerald-500 {{ $class ?? 'h-5 w-5' }}"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <span class="absolute -top-0.5 left-1/2 h-1.5 w-1.5 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
</span>
